AVIF written at 8 or 10 bits. SVT-AV1, the only AV1 encoder of the libheif of az,
writes 8 and 10 bits ("Svt[error]: Encoder Bit Depth shall be only 8 or 10"), and
ImageMagick gave it 12 for an image deeper than 10 bits: a canvas of xc: at the
quantum depth (16) with 8-bit pixels composited on it, as the video sites make
their screenshots and the preview of the player, or a 16-bit PNG; the write failed
("IM operation failed", the task of the site cancelled). Now a frame of 9 to 12 bits
(a 10-bit HEIC or AVIF, -depth 10) goes as 10 bits, a deeper one (16: the quantum
depth of a canvas of xc: and of what is composited on it, a 16-bit PNG) as 8, as
-depth 8 makes it and as the sites show it; 8 bits or less as they are.
--- a/coders/heic.c
+++ b/coders/heic.c
@@ -2518,6 +2518,20 @@
   heif_context=heif_context_alloc();
   encode_avif=(LocaleCompare(image_info->magick,"AVIF") == 0) ? MagickTrue :
     MagickFalse;
+  if (encode_avif != MagickFalse)
+    {
+      Image
+        *frame;
+
+      /*
+        SVT-AV1, the AV1 encoder of libheif here, writes 8 and 10 bits only:
+        9 to 12 bits as 10, deeper (the quantum depth of a canvas of xc: and
+        of a 16-bit PNG) as 8.
+      */
+      for (frame=image; frame != (Image *) NULL; frame=GetNextImageInList(frame))
+        if (frame->depth > 8)
+          frame->depth=frame->depth <= 12 ? 10 : 8;
+    }
 #if LIBHEIF_NUMERIC_VERSION >= HEIC_COMPUTE_NUMERIC_VERSION(1,20,0)
   if ((encode_avif != MagickFalse) && (image_info->adjoin != MagickFalse) &&
       (GetNextImageInList(image) != (Image *) NULL))
